tem information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3080 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9186) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-12900K (24 threads) - 63.78 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen the object is in read-only state the inspector allow deleting metadata (but correctly prevent adding or editing metadata)\n\n<img width=\"491\" height=\"469\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/429d35e2-06d0-4a21-bcde-ee70fe8226e4\" />\n\nThe easier way to reproduce the issue was to use the undocumented `_is_read_only` virtual method (See https://github.com/godotengine/godot-docs/issues/11794)\n\nThe `_is_read_only` method is currently only used in the animator but I did not find a way to reproduce the issue in there because the metadata are also hidden with the function `_hide_metadata_from_inspector`\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Add a simple GDScript ;\n```gdscript\n@tool\nextends Node\nclass_name TestNode\n\n@export var foo: String = \"bar\"\n\n\nfunc _is_read_only() -> bool:\n\treturn false\n```\n- Add a metadata\n- Edit the `_is_read_only` function so it's returning true\n- Notice that you can delete the metadata added in previous step but can't add or edit it.\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp_read_only_2026-02-27_13-45-23.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25604306/mrp_read_only_2026-02-27_13-45-23.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","su